  "query_preview": "../Wednesday through Friday/...\nGenerally uneventful weather pattern in the extended portion of \nthe forecast, wrapping up October neatly. A ridge of high pressure\nin the Gulf will be the main feature driving the weather in SE \nAK. Offshore flow will lead to milder weather and limited to no \nprecipitation for much of this week. Early in the week, the \nfeature most worthy of discussing is a small low which intensifies\na bit over the southern panhandle and move further south. This \nwill amp up the N-S pressure gradient on Tuesday into Wednesday, \nincreasing northerly winds in Lynn Canal, and potentially other \nN-S inner channels to a lesser extent.\n\nLater in the week on Friday the next considerable low and \nattendant fronts will be moving into the Gulf, raising rain \nchances yet again.",
